{"depth":"full","paper_type":"archival_reuse","paper_type_evidence":[{"loc":"2.1 Analysis of Archival Data","quote":"We used the archival data of the 0.87 mm dust polarization from the protoplanetary disk around HD 163296 (2015.1.00616.S; PI: C. Pinte)."}],"fields":["protoplanetary_disks"],"question":{"value":"What grain sizes and dust scale heights, as a function of radius, reproduce the resolved 0.87 mm self-scattering polarization of the HD 163296 disk, and what do they imply for turbulence?","evidence":[{"loc":"abstract","quote":"we conduct radiative transfer modeling that includes self-scattering polarization to constrain the grain size and its distribution."}]},"targets":[{"name":"HD 163296","details":[{"loc":"1 Introduction","quote":"The distance was derived to be 101.5 pc by (cite: gai18; bai18)."}],"coordinates":"not stated","redshift_or_distance":"101.5 pc","distance_source":"Gaia (gai18; bai18)"}],"alma_project_codes":[{"code":"2015.1.00616.S","evidence":[{"loc":"2.1 Analysis of Archival Data","quote":"We used the archival data of the 0.87 mm dust polarization from the protoplanetary disk around HD 163296 (2015.1.00616.S; PI: C. Pinte)."}]}],"data_settings":[{"field":"bands","value":"0.87 mm (Band 7) dust polarization","evidence":[{"loc":"2.1 Analysis of Archival Data","quote":"We used the archival data of the 0.87 mm dust polarization from the protoplanetary disk around HD 163296"}]},{"field":"angular_resolution","value":"0.20" x 0.18" (~20x18 au)","evidence":[{"loc":"2.1 Analysis of Archival Data","quote":"The beam size of the final product was $0.20\ensuremath{''}\times0.18\ensuremath{''}$, corresponding to a spatial resolution of $\sim20\times18$ au"}]},{"field":"pi_or_archival_as_stated","value":"Archival, PI C. Pinte; originally presented by Dent et al. 2019","evidence":[{"loc":"2.1 Analysis of Archival Data","quote":"These data were originally presented by (cite: den19)."}]}],"lines_targeted":[],"other_facilities":[],"external_data_from_literature":[{"what":{"value":"Temperature profile T=220 K (R/1au)^-0.5","evidence":[{"loc":"3 Disk Model","quote":"We adopted the following temperature profile with a smooth power law distribution derived by (cite: ise16)"}]},"citation":"(cite: ise16)"},{"what":{"value":"Inclination 47 deg and position angle 133.3 deg from DSHARP","evidence":[{"loc":"3 Disk Model","quote":"The inclination and position angle were assumed to be $47^\circ$ and 133.3$^\circ$, respectively, as derived by the DSHARP project (cite: ise18)."}]},"citation":"(cite: ise18)"},{"what":{"value":"Gas surface density 3-10 g cm^-2 in 50 au gap and 0.1-2 g cm^-2 in 90 au gap from CO lines","evidence":[{"loc":"6.2 Estimate of turbulence strength","quote":"The gas surface density has been constrained by multiple CO line observations to be $3-10 {\rm~g~cm^{-2}}$ in the 50 au gap and $0.1-2 {\rm~g~cm^{-2}}$ in the 90 au gap (cite: ise16)."}]},"citation":"(cite: ise16)"},{"what":{"value":"Spectral index from 0.87 and 1.3 mm continuum","evidence":[{"loc":"6.1 Distributions of dust grains","quote":"(cite: den19) derived the spectral index, $\alpha$, using the ALMA 0.87 and 1.3 mm dust continuum observations"}]},"citation":"(cite: den19)"}],"simulations_or_models_as_data":[],"calibration":[{"field":"pipeline_or_manual","value":"Standard manual-style reduction in CASA, plus phase and amplitude self-calibration","evidence":[{"loc":"2.1 Analysis of Archival Data","quote":"The reduction and calibration of the data were done with CASA version 4.5.3 (cite: mcm07) in a standard manner."}]},{"field":"casa_version","value":"CASA 4.5.3","evidence":[{"loc":"2.1 Analysis of Archival Data","quote":"The reduction and calibration of the data were done with CASA version 4.5.3 (cite: mcm07) in a standard manner."}]},{"field":"self_calibration","value":"Phase and amplitude self-calibration performed","evidence":[{"loc":"2.1 Analysis of Archival Data","quote":"self-calibration for both phase and amplitude was performed."}]}],"imaging":[{"field":"task","value":"CASA tclean","evidence":[{"loc":"2.1 Analysis of Archival Data","quote":"Stokes images were reconstructed using the CASA task tCLEAN, with Briggs weighting with a robust parameter of 0.5."}]},{"field":"weighting_robust","value":"Briggs, robust = 0.5","evidence":[{"loc":"2.1 Analysis of Archival Data","quote":"Stokes images were reconstructed using the CASA task tCLEAN, with Briggs weighting with a robust parameter of 0.5."}]},{"field":"cell_size","value":"0.02 arcsec","evidence":[{"loc":"2.1 Analysis of Archival Data","quote":"The pixel size was set to $0.02\ensuremath{''}$."}]},{"field":"final_beam","value":"0.20" x 0.18"","evidence":[{"loc":"2.1 Analysis of Archival Data","quote":"The beam size of the final product was $0.20\ensuremath{''}\times0.18\ensuremath{''}$"}]},{"field":"final_rms","value":"sigma_Q=1.7e-5, sigma_U=3.0e-5, sigma_PI=4.0e-5 Jy/beam","evidence":[{"loc":"2.1 Analysis of Archival Data","quote":"$\sigma_{\it Q}=1.7\times10^{-5}$ Jy beam$^{-1}$, $\sigma_{\it U}=3.0\times10^{-5}$ Jy beam$^{-1}$, and $\sigma_{\rm PI}=4.0\times10^{-5}$ Jy beam$^{-1}$"}]}],"inherited":[{"what":{"value":"Opacity calculation follows Kataoka et al. 2016","evidence":[{"loc":"3 Disk Model","quote":"The calculation of opacity followed that by (cite: kat16)."}]},"from_reference":"(cite: kat16)"},{"what":{"value":"Multiple scattering in RADMC-3D as done by Kataoka et al. 2015","evidence":[{"loc":"3 Disk Model","quote":"taking into account multiple scattering, as done by (cite: kat15)"}]},"from_reference":"(cite: kat15)"},{"what":{"value":"Further flagging and calibration details in Dent et al. 2019","evidence":[{"loc":"2.1 Analysis of Archival Data","quote":"Note that (cite: den19) examined the calibrated data in more detail, and applied further flagging."}]},"from_reference":"(cite: den19)"}],"unstated_but_needed":["Observing dates, configurations, baselines, spectral setup and on-source time","Self-calibration solution intervals and reference images","Flagging details, calibrators and flux scale uncertainty","Deconvolution settings (masking, threshold, niter) and image size","RADMC-3D photon numbers, grid setup, stellar parameters and gas scale height/temperature setup","Method of extracting radial profiles along major and minor axes and how model-data agreement was judged","Minimum grain size for the two-population model and gas-to-dust ratio"],"analysis_steps":[{"order":1,"goal":"Image Stokes I, Q, U and build polarization fraction map","method":{"value":"tclean imaging of archival data, debiased PI, Pfrac=PI/I above 3 sigma_PI","evidence":[{"loc":"2.1 Analysis of Archival Data","quote":"We thus debiased the polarized intensity map as $PI=\sqrt{Q^2+U^2-\sigma_{\rm PI}^2}$."}]},"software":["CASA"],"key_parameters":[{"value":"robust 0.5, 0.02" pixels","evidence":[{"loc":"2.1 Analysis of Archival Data","quote":"The pixel size was set to $0.02\ensuremath{''}$."}]}],"assumptions":[{"value":"Stokes V ignored","evidence":[{"loc":"2.1 Analysis of Archival Data","quote":"Note that we ignore the Stokes *V* component in this study because it has not been well characterized for ALMA."}]}],"fitting":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"Compared with Dent et al. 2019 images","evidence":[{"loc":"2.2 Results","quote":"These images are consistent with those obtained by (cite: den19)."}]}},{"order":2,"goal":"Build axisymmetric dust disk model reproducing continuum","method":{"value":"Optical depth profile with ring Gaussians at 70, 104, 160 au; I=(1-e^-tau)B(Td); Sigma_dust=tau/kappa_abs","evidence":[{"loc":"3 Disk Model","quote":"The surface density is derived with the assumption that $\tau=\kappa_{\rm abs}\times\Sigma_{\rm dust}$"}]},"software":[],"key_parameters":[{"value":"Td=220 K (R/1au)^-0.5","evidence":[{"loc":"3 Disk Model","quote":"$$\begin{equation}
T_{d}= 220\ {\rm K}\ \Big(\frac{R}{1\ {\rm au}}\Big)^{-0.5}. 
\label{temp}
\end{equation}$$"}]}],"assumptions":[{"value":"Spherical grains, q=-3.5, Mie theory, 50% silicate / 50% water ice, Maxwell-Garnett mixing","evidence":[{"loc":"3 Disk Model","quote":"The composition was assumed to be a mixture of silicate (50%) and water ice (50%)"}]}],"fitting":{"value":"Hand-tuned profile; no formal fit","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"Model intensity profile on major axis compared to data","evidence":[{"loc":"3 Disk Model","quote":"The figure confirms that the model reproduces the continuum image."}]}},{"order":3,"goal":"Radiative transfer of self-scattering polarization","method":{"value":"RADMC-3D with multiple scattering; Stokes I,Q,U convolved with 0.2" Gaussian beam","evidence":[{"loc":"3 Disk Model","quote":"The Stokes *I*, *Q*, and *U* images were convolved with a Gaussian beam with a full width at half maximum (FWHM) of $0.2\ensuremath{''}$ to produce the final model images."}]},"software":["RADMC-3D"],"key_parameters":[{"value":"inclination 47 deg, PA 133.3 deg","evidence":[{"loc":"3 Disk Model","quote":"The inclination and position angle were assumed to be $47^\circ$ and 133.3$^\circ$, respectively"}]}],"assumptions":[{"value":"Gaussian vertical distribution with h_d=h_g/f_set; polarization only from self-scattering","evidence":[{"loc":"3 Disk Model","quote":"We set an additional dust settling parameter $f_{\rm set}$ such that $h_d=h_g/f_{\rm set}$"}]}],"fitting":{"value":"Grid of models varying a_max, population mass ratio and f_set; compared by eye/profiles","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"Compared radial Pfrac profiles along axes and Stokes Q/U maps","evidence":[{"loc":"5.4 Radial variation of dust scale height","quote":"We compare the images not only for the polarization fraction but also for the Stokes *Q* and *U* distributions."}]}},{"order":4,"goal":"Constrain grain populations and dust scale height by radius","method":{"value":"Single population then two populations (140 um and 1 mm); Stokes Q upper limit sets H_dust; best: f_set=10 for r<=68 au, 1.5 beyond","evidence":[{"loc":"5.4 Radial variation of dust scale height","quote":"To reproduce the observations, we apply $f_{\rm set}=10$ within $r\leq68$ au and $f_{\rm set}=1.5$ for $r>68$ au."}]},"software":["RADMC-3D"],"key_parameters":[{"value":"1 mm grains within +-5 au of ring centers; 5.5:4.5 mixture at r<=40 au","evidence":[{"loc":"5.2 Model with Two Dust Grain Populations","quote":"We set a ratio of surface density (and density) of $5.5:4.5$ (corresponding to a ratio of $11/9$) between the 140 $\mu$m and 1 mm dust grain populations"}]}],"assumptions":[],"fitting":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"Single-population model with variable f_set fails to reproduce Q","evidence":[{"loc":"8 Additional Test of Model with Single Grain Population","quote":"Therefore, a model with a single grain population is unlikely to explain the observations even if the dust scale height is changed."}]}},{"order":5,"goal":"Derive turbulence alpha in gaps","method":{"value":"Settling-diffusion balance H_dust formula with Stokes number from gas surface density","evidence":[{"loc":"6.2 Estimate of turbulence strength","quote":"By assuming a balance between vertical settling and turbulent diffusion, the dust scale height is written as (cite: dub95; you07)"}]},"software":[],"key_parameters":[],"assumptions":[{"value":"Dust material density 1.67 g cm^-3; CO abundance 5e-5 for gas surface density","evidence":[{"loc":"6.2 Estimate of turbulence strength","quote":"assuming that the dust material density is $\rho\sim1.67$ g cm$^{-3}$"}]}],"fitting":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"Compared with molecular-line turbulence limits","evidence":[{"loc":"6.2 Estimate of turbulence strength","quote":"The low value of $\alpha\lesssim1.5\times10^{-3}$ inside the 70 au ring is consistent with the upper limit derived from molecular line observations"}]}}],"software":[{"name":"CASA","version":"4.5.3","used_for":{"value":"Calibration and tclean imaging","evidence":[{"loc":"2.1 Analysis of Archival Data","quote":"The reduction and calibration of the data were done with CASA version 4.5.3 (cite: mcm07) in a standard manner."}]}},{"name":"RADMC-3D","version":"not stated","used_for":{"value":"Radiative transfer including scattering polarization","evidence":[{"loc":"3 Disk Model","quote":"We performed radiative transfer calculations with RADMC-3D[^1] (cite: dul12) taking into account multiple scattering"}]}}],"results_numeric":[{"quantity":"Polarization fraction at center","value":"~0.8","uncertainty":"0.04","units":"%","from_step":1,"evidence":[{"loc":"2.2 Results","quote":"The polarization fraction is $\sim0.8\pm0.04$% in the center"}]},{"quantity":"Polarization fraction in 50 au gap","value":"~2.3","uncertainty":"0.5","units":"%","from_step":1,"evidence":[{"loc":"2.2 Results","quote":"increases to $\sim2.3\pm0.5$% in the first gap at 50 au"}]},{"quantity":"Polarization fraction in 90 au gap","value":"~3","uncertainty":"0.7","units":"%","from_step":1,"evidence":[{"loc":"2.2 Results","quote":"to $\sim3\pm0.7$% in the second gap at 90 au along the major axis"}]},{"quantity":"Maximum grain size in gaps","value":"140","uncertainty":"not stated","units":"micron","from_step":4,"evidence":[{"loc":"abstract","quote":"The maximum grain size was 140 microns in the gaps and significantly larger or smaller in the rings."}]},{"quantity":"H_dust/H_gas inside 70 au ring","value":"<~1/3","uncertainty":"3 sigma upper limit","units":"dimensionless","from_step":4,"evidence":[{"loc":"5.4 Radial variation of dust scale height","quote":"we can set the upper limit of the dust scale height as $H_{\rm dust}\lesssim (1/3)H_{\rm gas}$"}]},{"quantity":"H_dust/H_gas outside 70 au ring","value":"~2/3","uncertainty":"not stated","units":"dimensionless","from_step":4,"evidence":[{"loc":"6.2 Estimate of turbulence strength","quote":"$H_{\rm dust}/H_{\rm gas}\sim2/3$ for the $r\gtrsim 70$ au region"}]},{"quantity":"alpha in 50 au gap","value":"<=1.5e-3","uncertainty":"upper limit","units":"dimensionless","from_step":5,"evidence":[{"loc":"6.2 Estimate of turbulence strength","quote":"$\alpha\lesssim 1.5\times10^{-3}$ in the 50 au gap"}]},{"quantity":"alpha in 90 au gap","value":"0.015-0.3","uncertainty":"range","units":"dimensionless","from_step":5,"evidence":[{"loc":"6.2 Estimate of turbulence strength","quote":"$\alpha\simeq0.015-0.3$ in the 90 au gap"}]},{"quantity":"St/alpha outside 70 au ring","value":"1.25","uncertainty":"not stated","units":"dimensionless","from_step":5,"evidence":[{"loc":"6.2 Estimate of turbulence strength","quote":"${\rm St}/\alpha \gtrsim 8$ inside the 70 au ring and ${\rm St}/\alpha \simeq 1.25$ outside the 70 au ring"}]}],"findings_qualitative":[{"value":"Dust scale height raises azimuthal polarization variation; grain size mainly sets polarization fraction and does not alter vectors.","evidence":[{"loc":"4.2 Dust Grain Size and Dust Scale Height Distribution","quote":"We can thus conclude that the grain size only affects the polarization fraction; it does not affect the polarization vectors in self-scattering."}]},{"value":"Turbulence transition at 70 au ring suggests a dead zone or e-heating zone.","evidence":[{"loc":"abstract","quote":"The transition of the turbulence strength at the boundary of the 70 au ring indicates the existence of a dead zone."}]}],"claims":[{"hypothesis":"Can a single grain population with constant settling reproduce the polarization?","experiment":"Radiative transfer with a_max=140 and 160 um and f_set 1-10","result":"Minor-axis Pfrac too high and Stokes Q mismatch","finding":"A single radially constant population cannot reproduce observations","support":"supported","evidence":[{"loc":"5.1 Single Grain Population","quote":"These models indicate that a model with a single grain population cannot reproduce the observations."}]},{"hypothesis":"Do grain size and dust scale height vary radially?","experiment":"Two-population model with 140 um in gaps, 1 mm in rings, f_set 10 inside and 1.5 outside 68 au","result":"Model matches Pfrac, Q and U images","finding":"Gaps host ~140 um grains; dust is thinner inside 70 au than outside","support":"supported","evidence":[{"loc":"5.4 Radial variation of dust scale height","quote":"The model well matches the observations not only for the polarization fraction but also for the Stokes *Q* and *U* images."}]},{"hypothesis":"Is turbulence different inside and outside the 70 au ring?","experiment":"Convert H_dust/H_gas and gap grain size into alpha","result":"alpha <=1.5e-3 vs 0.015-0.3","finding":"Order-of-magnitude turbulence difference, suggesting a dead zone","support":"partially","evidence":[{"loc":"6.2 Estimate of turbulence strength","quote":"Yet, the difference of an order of magnitude in turbulence strength between the inner and outer regions is robust."}]}],"reasoning":[{"field":"why_this_method","value":"Radiative transfer needed to interpret resolved self-scattering polarization in terms of dust properties.","evidence":[{"loc":"1 Introduction","quote":"In this study, we perform radiative transfer modeling to determine what can be constrained based on spatially resolved polarimetric observations."}]}],"alternatives_considered_or_rejected":[{"value":"Single grain population with varied scale height rejected; larger or smaller grains instead of the mixture considered possible (~170 or ~80 um).","evidence":[{"loc":"5.2 Model with Two Dust Grain Populations","quote":"Note that it is also possible to explain the lower polarization fraction by assuming a slightly larger ($\sim170$ $\mu$m) or smaller dust grain size ($\sim80$ $\mu$m)"}]}],"limitations_admitted":[{"value":"Polarization assumed to be only self-scattering; alignment contributions could change the interpretation.","evidence":[{"loc":"6.4 Caveats of models","quote":"Another caveat is that the polarization is assumed to be produced only by self-scattering."}]},{"value":"Grain size in rings is not constrained beyond being far from 140 um.","evidence":[{"loc":"6.4 Caveats of models","quote":"it is possible that dust grains much larger or smaller than 140 $\mu$m are distributed in the rings rather than the 1 mm dust grain population."}]}],"referee_caveats_inferred":["Model comparison is qualitative with no formal fit or uncertainties on grain size and f_set","Results depend on assumed composition, opacity and fixed temperature profile","Alpha estimates rely on uncertain CO-based gas surface densities","Self-scattering only; alignment effects not tested"],"reproducibility":[{"field":"data_public_as_stated","value":"Archival ALMA data, project 2015.1.00616.S","evidence":[{"loc":"2.1 Analysis of Archival Data","quote":"We used the archival data of the 0.87 mm dust polarization from the protoplanetary disk around HD 163296 (2015.1.00616.S; PI: C. Pinte)."}]}],"code_released":[],"missing_for_reproduction":["Self-calibration parameters and flagging","RADMC-3D setup details (grid, photons, stellar parameters)","Profile extraction and comparison procedure"],"estimated_data_volume_inferred":"~50-150 GB raw for a polarization Band 7 dataset","score_inferred":3,"score_reason":"Public data and a clear model description, but imaging, self-calibration and RADMC-3D setup are incomplete, and the model comparison is not quantitative.","rediscovery_candidate":false,"rediscovery_reason":"Main results come from hand-tuned forward models that are compared qualitatively, so they cannot be redone from a complete recipe.","methods_papers":[{"citation":"(cite: kat16)","why":"Opacity and self-scattering polarization modeling"},{"citation":"(cite: kat15)","why":"RADMC-3D multiple-scattering polarization approach"}],"companion_papers":[{"citation":"(cite: den19)","why":"Original presentation of the ALMA polarization data"},{"citation":"(cite: ise18)","why":"DSHARP HD 163296 geometry and ring structure"}],"related_projects_or_surveys":["DSHARP"]}
